msgid "**Admin user creation:** inserts the admin user directly into the ``users`` table, bypassing email verification. Idempotent via ``WHERE NOT EXISTS``."
msgstr "**Vytvorenie administrátora:** vloží administrátora priamo do ``users`` tabuľka, obídenie overenie e-mailu. Idempotentná prostredníctvom ``WHERE NOT EXISTS``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Admin user creation:** inserts the admin user directly into the `users` table, bypassing email verification. Idempotent via `WHERE NOT EXISTS`."
msgstr "**Vytvorenie administrátora:** vloží administrátora priamo do `users` tabuľka, obídenie overenie e-mailu. Idempotentná prostredníctvom `WHERE NOT EXISTS`."

msgid "**Admin-gated consoles:** Both interfaces are reachable only for members of the administrator group."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator Password:** The superuser password converges to the configured administrator's password on every deploy. An installed Matomo that lacks the configured administrator gets it as a further superuser next to the existing ones."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator Password:** The superuser password converges to the configured administrator’s password on every deploy. An installed Matomo that lacks the configured administrator gets it as a further superuser next to the existing ones."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator Role Mapping:** Members of the ``administrator`` role group are Nextcloud administrators. With LDAP, ``user_ldap`` reads the role group as its admin group at runtime and a change reaches Nextcloud within ``NEXTCLOUD_LDAP_CACHE_TTL`` seconds; with ``sociallogin``, the groups claim maps to the ``admin`` group at every login; with ``oidc_login`` outside the LDAP proxy mode, the ``is_admin`` attribute reads the groups claim."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator Role Mapping:** Members of the `administrator` role group are Nextcloud administrators. With LDAP, `user_ldap` reads the role group as its admin group at runtime and a change reaches Nextcloud within `NEXTCLOUD_LDAP_CACHE_TTL` seconds; with `sociallogin`, the groups claim maps to the `admin` group at every login; with `oidc_login` outside the LDAP proxy mode, the `is_admin` attribute reads the groups claim."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator group:** The group ``web-app-proxmox-administrator`` holds the ``Administrator`` role on ``/``, propagated. Proxmox VE accepts only ``[A-Za-z0-9._-]`` in an OpenID group claim, so the role cannot map the full-path RBAC claim; instead the RBAC sync (``tasks/utils/rbac/sync.yml``) adds every member of the Keycloak administrator group to it, at deploy and on its timer, and removes every other account from it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator group:** The group `web-app-proxmox-administrator` holds the `Administrator` role on `/`, propagated. Proxmox VE accepts only `[A-Za-z0-9._-]` in an OpenID group claim, so the role cannot map the full-path RBAC claim; instead the RBAC sync (`tasks/utils/rbac/sync.yml`) adds every member of the Keycloak administrator group to it, at deploy and on its timer, and removes every other account from it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Administrator login is enforced to be key-based:** playbooks fail early if users.administrator.authorized_keys is empty."
msgstr "**Prihlásenie správcu sa požaduje na základe kľúča:** playbooky zlyhajú skôr, ak users.administrator.authorized_keys je prázdny."

msgid "**Administrator reconcile:** [reconcile_admins.rb](./files/ruby/reconcile_admins.rb) grants OpenProject administrator rights to the members of the `administrator` role group, provisions those that have no account yet from LDAP, and revokes the rights from every other account except the platform administrator and the GitLab bot. It runs as a container hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) at every deploy and on its timer, so a group change in Keycloak or LDAP reaches `User.admin` within one timer interval."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator reconcile:** `reconcile_admins.rb <./files/ruby/reconcile_admins.rb>`__ grants OpenProject administrator rights to the members of the ``administrator`` role group, provisions those that have no account yet from LDAP, and revokes the rights from every other account except the platform administrator and the GitLab bot. It runs as a container hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ at every deploy and on its timer, so a group change in Keycloak or LDAP reaches ``User.admin`` within one timer interval."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator role from the IdP:** every realm user may sign in; members of the ``administrator`` RBAC group of ``web-app-jellyfin`` get the Jellyfin administrator flag. The SSO plugin reads it from the ``groups`` claim, the LDAP plugin from the ``memberOf`` entry of the group, and both remove the flag at the next login of a user who left the group."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator role from the IdP:** every realm user may sign in; members of the `administrator` RBAC group of `web-app-jellyfin` get the Jellyfin administrator flag. The SSO plugin reads it from the `groups` claim, the LDAP plugin from the `memberOf` entry of the group, and both remove the flag at the next login of a user who left the group."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator role:** [files/ruby/greenlight/reconcile_roles.rb](./files/ruby/greenlight/reconcile_roles.rb) sets the Greenlight `Administrator` role from the `web-app-bigbluebutton` `administrator` members, matched by email, and demotes every other Greenlight administrator to `User`, as an RBAC hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) at every deploy and on its timer. The platform administrator keeps the role."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator role:** `files/ruby/greenlight/reconcile_roles.rb <./files/ruby/greenlight/reconcile_roles.rb>`__ sets the Greenlight ``Administrator`` role from the ``web-app-bigbluebutton`` ``administrator`` members, matched by email, and demotes every other Greenlight administrator to ``User``, as an RBAC hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ at every deploy and on its timer. The platform administrator keeps the role."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Administrator-issued token:** The role mints a Gitea personal access token named ``gitea-mcp`` for the ``administrator`` account with the read-only scope set ``read:repository,read:issue,read:user,read:organization,read:notification``, and persists it in the token store MCP clients read. Every deploy asks the API whether the stored token still authenticates, revokes the stale entry under that name, and re-mints when the API rejects it. The deploy fails if the fresh token is rejected too."
msgstr "**Token vydaný administrátorom:** Úloha mincovne a Gitea osobný prístup k tokenu s názvom ``gitea-mcp`` pre ``administrator`` účet so súborom len na čítanie ``read:repository,read:issue,read:user,read:organization,read:notification``, a pretrváva v symbolickom obchode MCP klientov čítať. Každé nasadenie žiada API či skladovaný token stále autentifikuje, zruší zablokovaný záznam pod týmto názvom a znovu uvedie, keď API Odmieta to. Nasadenie zlyhá, ak je čerstvý token tiež odmietnutý."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Administrator-issued token:** The role mints a Gitea personal access token named `gitea-mcp` for the `administrator` account with the read-only scope set `read:repository,read:issue,read:user,read:organization,read:notification`, and persists it in the token store MCP clients read. Every deploy asks the API whether the stored token still authenticates, revokes the stale entry under that name, and re-mints when the API rejects it. The deploy fails if the fresh token is rejected too."
msgstr "**Token vydaný administrátorom:** Úloha mincovne a Gitea osobný prístup k tokenu s názvom `gitea-mcp` pre `administrator` účet so súborom len na čítanie `read:repository,read:issue,read:user,read:organization,read:notification`, a pretrváva v symbolickom obchode MCP klientov čítať. Každé nasadenie žiada API či skladovaný token stále autentifikuje, zruší zablokovaný záznam pod týmto názvom a znovu uvedie, keď API Odmieta to. Nasadenie zlyhá, ak je čerstvý token tiež odmietnutý."

msgid "**Administrator:** blocked only with ``sso`` off. The shared native login looks the username field up by the names ``username``, ``email`` and ``login``, while Matomo names it ``form_login``, so the persona would submit the password alone. ``files/playwright/auth.spec.js`` drives the native form of the local superuser. With ``sso`` on the persona clicks the RebelOIDC button and signs in through Keycloak; ``files/playwright/addons/rebeloidc.spec.js`` additionally asserts the superuser access and the Keycloak sign-out."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrator:** blocked only with `sso` off. The shared native login looks the username field up by the names `username`, `email` and `login`, while Matomo names it `form_login`, so the persona would submit the password alone. `files/playwright/auth.spec.js` drives the native form of the local superuser. With `sso` on the persona clicks the RebelOIDC button and signs in through Keycloak; `files/playwright/addons/rebeloidc.spec.js` additionally asserts the superuser access and the Keycloak sign-out."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrators and domain managers:** [files/python/rbac_sync.py](./files/python/rbac_sync.py) sets `global_admin` from the `web-app-mailu` `administrator` members and the managers of the mail domain from the `domain-manager` members through the Mailu REST API inside the admin container. Members are promoted, every other global administrator and domain manager is demoted. The platform administrator stays a global administrator. It runs as a host hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) at every deploy and on its timer."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrators and domain managers:** `files/python/rbac_sync.py <./files/python/rbac_sync.py>`__ sets ``global_admin`` from the ``web-app-mailu`` ``administrator`` members and the managers of the mail domain from the ``domain-manager`` members through the Mailu REST API inside the admin container. Members are promoted, every other global administrator and domain manager is demoted. The platform administrator stays a global administrator. It runs as a host hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ at every deploy and on its timer."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrators:** System Administrator follows the ``web-app-stalwart`` ``administrator`` members. `files/python/rbac_sync.py <./files/python/rbac_sync.py>`__ grants and revokes it through the management JMAP API as a host hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__, at every SSO deploy and on its timer, so a member who signs in for the first time gets it on the next run. The recovery administrator ``stalwartadmin`` and the platform administrator keep it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Administrators:** System Administrator follows the `web-app-stalwart` `administrator` members. [files/python/rbac_sync.py](./files/python/rbac_sync.py) grants and revokes it through the management JMAP API as a host hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/), at every SSO deploy and on its timer, so a member who signs in for the first time gets it on the next run. The recovery administrator `stalwartadmin` and the platform administrator keep it."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Advanced Analytics:** Gain insights through detailed reporting on campaign metrics and subscriber behavior."
msgstr "**Pokročilá analýza:** Získajte prehľady prostredníctvom podrobného podávania správ o ukazovateľoch kampane a správania účastníkov."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Advanced Rights Management:** Fine-grained permissions for users, groups, and spaces."
msgstr "**Pokročilé riadenie práv:** Jemné práva pre užívateľov, skupiny a priestory."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Advanced SEO Tools:** Optimize your site's visibility in search engines using built-in support for SEO best practices and a rich ecosystem of SEO plugins."
msgstr "**Pokročilé SEO Nástroje:** Optimalizovať viditeľnosť vašich stránok vo vyhľadávačoch pomocou vstavanej podpory pre SEO najlepšie postupy a bohatý ekosystém SEO pluginy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Advanced SEO Tools:** Optimize your site’s visibility in search engines using built-in support for SEO best practices and a rich ecosystem of SEO plugins."
msgstr "**Pokročilé SEO Nástroje:** Optimalizovať svoje stránky a viditeľnosť vo vyhľadávačoch pomocou vstavanej podpory pre SEO najlepšie postupy a bohatý ekosystém SEO pluginy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Advanced Security Options:** Benefit from multi-factor authentication, configurable password policies, and secure session management."
msgstr "**Pokročilé možnosti zabezpečenia:** Využite viacfaktorovú autentifikáciu, konfigurovateľné zásady hesla a bezpečnú správu sedenia."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Advanced Security:** Incorporates TLS encryption, DKIM, and SPF to secure your communications and prevent spoofing."
msgstr "**Pokročilá bezpečnosť:** Začlení TLS šifrovanie, DKIM, a SPF pre zabezpečenie vašej komunikácie a zabrániť Spoofing."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Advanced openresty load-balancing strategies.** v1 uses default round-robin in the per-app `upstream` block. Weighted distribution, least-connections, sticky sessions (`ip_hash` / cookie-based), and active HTTP healthchecks are out of scope. Adding them is a follow-up requirement and only becomes load-bearing once a service is regularly run with replicas > 1, which itself depends on shared storage being NFS-backed for that service."
msgstr "**Pokročilé stratégie vyrovnávania zaťaženia.** v1 používa predvolený okrúhly robín v jednom app `upstream` blok. Vážená distribúcia, najmenšie spojenia, lepkavé sedenia (`ip_hash` / cookie-based), a aktívne HTTP zdravotné kontroly sú mimo rozsah. Pridanie je následná požiadavka a stáva sa nositeľom až vtedy, keď sa služba pravidelne vykonáva s replikami > 1, ktorý sám o sebe závisí od zdieľaného úložiska, ktoré je pre túto službu podporované NFS."

msgid "**Agent VM template:** ``files/vm-template/`` holds the package list and the ``rootfs/`` tree of the agent VM image that ``make agents-vm-template`` builds. The build checks the sha256 of every runtime tarball and of ``act`` it downloads, refuses a sum that is not 64 lowercase hex digits, and installs the runtimes with ``npm install --ignore-scripts``. Known gap, dependencies unverified: npm resolves the dependencies of each runtime tarball from the registry without a lockfile or a checked sum."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Agent VM template:** `files/vm-template/` holds the package list and the `rootfs/` tree of the agent VM image that `make agents-vm-template` builds. The build checks the sha256 of every runtime tarball and of `act` it downloads, refuses a sum that is not 64 lowercase hex digits, and installs the runtimes with `npm install --ignore-scripts`. Known gap, dependencies unverified: npm resolves the dependencies of each runtime tarball from the registry without a lockfile or a checked sum."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Agent bridge:** ``services.incus.network`` is a bridge without NAT and without IPv6, so a VM leaves the host only through the egress proxy the agent firewall compiles."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Agent bridge:** `services.incus.network` is a bridge without NAT and without IPv6, so a VM leaves the host only through the egress proxy the agent firewall compiles."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent dashboards are public behind proxy + Keycloak OIDC.** `web-app-hermes` and `web-app-openclaw` follow the standard `web-app-*` contract: own canonical domain, reverse-proxy routing, SSO enforced via [`web-app-keycloak`](../../roles/web-app-keycloak/). Hermes uses its native self-hosted OIDC support. OpenClaw's native OIDC is unverified upstream: if absent, the dashboard sits behind the platform's standard auth-proxy pattern (SSO enforced at the proxy, OpenClaw's own token auth staying internal-only). No unauthenticated public surface either way."
msgstr "**Pomôcky agenta sú verejné za proxy + Keycloak OIDC.** `web-app-hermes` a `web-app-openclaw` dodržiavať normu `web-app-*` zmluva: vlastná kanonická doména, spätná väzba, SSO vynútená prostredníctvom [`web-app-keycloak`](../../roles/web-app-keycloak/). Hermes používa svoju vlastnú podporu OIDC. OpenClaw je rodák OIDC je neoverený proti prúdu: ak chýba, palubná doska sedí za štandardnou auth-proxy vzor platformy (SSO presadzované na splnomocnenci, OpenClaw's own token auth staying internal-only)V žiadnom prípade žiadny neautentický verejný povrch."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent gateway:** The container runs the OpenClaw gateway bound to the LAN interface on port 18789, with an HTTP health check against `/healthz`."
msgstr "**Brána agenta:** Kontajner vedie OpenClaw brána viazaná na rozhranie LAN v prístave 18789, so zdravotnou kontrolou HTTP proti `/healthz`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent gateway:** The container runs the OpenClaw gateway bound to the LAN interface on port 18789, with an HTTP health check against ``/healthz``."
msgstr "**Brána agenta:** Kontajner vedie OpenClaw brána viazaná na rozhranie LAN v prístave 18789, so zdravotnou kontrolou HTTP proti ``/healthz``."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent receiver:** Container port 8000 is mapped to a host port (``local.agent``); external proxying for remote-host TLS agent registration is a follow-up."
msgstr "**Agent prijímač:** Prístav kontajnera 8000 je mapovaný do hostiteľského prístavu (``local.agent``); externé proxy pre registráciu agenta vzdialeného-hostiteľa TLS je následná kontrola."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent receiver:** Container port 8000 is mapped to a host port (`local.agent`); external proxying for remote-host TLS agent registration is a follow-up."
msgstr "**Agent prijímač:** Prístav kontajnera 8000 je mapovaný do hostiteľského prístavu (`local.agent`); externé proxy pre registráciu agenta vzdialeného-hostiteľa TLS je následná kontrola."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent reuse:** The embodied deployment is the agent role itself, so image, configuration and model routing stay identical to the isolated deployments."
msgstr "**Opätovné použitie činidla:** Stelesneným nasadením je samotná úloha agenta, takže obraz, konfigurácia a smerovanie modelov zostávajú identické s izolovanými nasadeniami."

msgid "**Agent sandbox.** *git commit --amend* is denied, the host's credential files stay unreadable inside the sandbox, sandboxed commands may reach local services on 127.0.0.1 to 127.0.0.12 and localhost, and third-party plugins are no longer switched on for every contributor."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agent-aware:** an agent role on the same host brings its editor extension along."
msgstr "**Agent:** rola agenta na tom istom hostiteľovi prináša rozšírenie vydavateľa."

msgid "**Agent-driven modelling:** An MCP client creates, edits and renders scenes through Blender's own Python API."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Agent-driven modelling:** An MCP client creates, edits and renders scenes through Blender’s own Python API."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agents as employees, with a kernel between them and the host.** *web-app-hermes* and *web-app-openclaw* deploy agents behind the single sign-on gate, wired to the gateway's models and to the MCP servers discovery hands them, each proving on deploy that it can actually reach them. *svc-virt-kata* runs that tier under a kernel-isolating container runtime, and *svc-ai-robot* embodies an agent on a dedicated device. Every sandboxed agent acts as its own platform account rather than borrowing yours. See [web-app-hermes](roles/web-app-hermes/README.md), [web-app-openclaw](roles/web-app-openclaw/README.md) and [svc-virt-kata](roles/svc-virt-kata/README.md)."
msgstr "**Agenti ako zamestnanci, s jadrom medzi nimi a hostiteľom.** *web-app-hermes* a *web-app-openclaw* rozmiestniť agentov za jedinou prihlasovacou bránou, napojených na modely brány a na MCP servery objavovať ich ruky, z ktorých každý dokazuje, že sa k nim môže dostať. *svc-virt-kata* prevádzkuje túto úroveň v rámci doby prevádzky nádoby s izoláciou jadra a *svc-ai-robot* stelesňuje agenta na vyhradenom zariadení. Každý sandboxed agent koná ako jeho vlastný účet na platforme, a nie požičiavať si vaše. Pozri [web-app-hermes](roles/web-app-hermes/README.md), [web-app-openclaw](roles/web-app-openclaw/README.md) a [svc-virt-kata](roles/svc-virt-kata/README.md)."

msgid "**Agents consume tools as MCP clients via the [050](050-mcp-role-integration.md) mechanism.** Hermes and OpenClaw are configured as MCP clients of the repository's MCP server roles over HTTP/SSE (not stdio: under microVM isolation and multi-node placement a stdio subprocess cannot reach an MCP server in another container). Discovery and credentials reuse 050's [`roles_with_service`](../../plugins/lookup/roles_with_service.py) lookup and `credentials:` blocks. Both roles are added to 050's MCP audit as client roles. Only 050's shared contract (the `services.mcp` schema) and the lookup extension are prerequisites for this requirement; 050's audit tooling, full lint set, and baserow+openwebui slice are independent later work."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agents on demand:** The first completion of a user for ``hermes`` or ``openclaw`` creates that user’s agent; later requests reuse it, and a stopped agent is started again with its state volume re-attached."
msgstr "**Pracovníci na požiadanie:** Prvé dokončenie užívateľa pre ``hermes`` alebo ``openclaw`` vytvára, že užívateľský agent; neskôr žiada o opätovné použitie, a zastavený agent sa začína znovu s jeho state objem znovu pripojený."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agents on demand:** The first completion of a user for `hermes` or `openclaw` creates that user's agent; later requests reuse it, and a stopped agent is started again with its state volume re-attached."
msgstr "**Pracovníci na požiadanie:** Prvé dokončenie užívateľa pre `hermes` alebo `openclaw` vytvára tento užívateľský agent; neskôr ho žiada o opätovné použitie, a zastavený agent sa začína znovu s jeho state hlasitosť znovu pripojené."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agents that spin up containers use nested Docker inside the isolated runtime; host socket passthrough is forbidden.** When an agent needs to run compose workloads (see the scenario below), it runs a nested Docker daemon inside its own isolated runtime. Mounting the host `/var/run/docker.sock` into an agent that executes model-generated code is **forbidden**: it grants root-equivalent host control and defeats the isolation entirely. Nested Docker costs performance and, on gVisor, may need `runsc` with the appropriate platform; the role README MUST document the overhead. An agent role that requires containers MUST declare this capability explicitly."
msgstr "**Agenti, ktorí roztočia kontajnery používať vnorené Docker vnútri izolovaného času; hostiteľ zásuvka priechod je zakázané.** Keď agent potrebuje spustiť skladať pracovné zaťaženie (Pozri ďalej uvedený scenár.), že vedie vnorené Docker démon vnútri svojho vlastného izolovaného času. Pripojenie hostiteľa `/var/run/docker.sock` do agenta, ktorý vykonáva modelový kód je **zakázané**: poskytuje koreňovo-ekvivalentné kontrolu hostiteľa a úplne porazí izoláciu. Nested Docker náklady výkon a, na gVisor, môže byť potrebné `runsc` s príslušnou platformou; úloha README MUSÍ dokumentovať režijné náklady. Úloha agenta, ktorá vyžaduje kontajnery MUSÍ vyhlásiť túto schopnosť výslovne."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Agile Boards & Scrum/Kanban Integration:** Manage agile projects using Scrum or Kanban boards, track progress through sprints, and maintain a clear overview of work in progress."
msgstr "**Agile Boards & Scrum/Kanban Integration:** Správa agilných projektov pomocou Scrum alebo Kanban dosky, sledovať pokrok prostredníctvom šprintov, a udržiavať jasný prehľad o práci v plnom prúde."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Alert rules live in the role that owns the metric.** A role ships its Prometheus rules in *templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2*. The new *alert_rule_roles* lookup includes them only for roles that Prometheus actually scrapes, so a rules file needs no activation check of its own. It must start at the *groups:* item level. OpenBao's seal alert is the first rule to use it."
msgstr "**Pravidlá varovania žijú v úlohe, ktorá vlastní metriku.** Úloha lodí jeho Prometheus pravidlá *templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2*Nový *alert_rule_roles* Hľadanie zahŕňa len pre úlohy, ktoré Prometheus Vlastne sa zoškrabuje, takže súbor pravidiel nepotrebuje aktivačnú kontrolu. Musí to začať na *skupiny:* úroveň položky. Otvoriť Baov poplach je prvé pravidlo, ktoré ho použije."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Alert rules ship with the role.** ``templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2`` is discovered by the ``alert_rule_roles`` lookup, which returns only roles that are actually scraped, so the fragment carries no activation guard of its own. It must start at the ``groups:`` item level."
msgstr "**Výstražné pravidlá sú na lodi s úlohou.** ``templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2`` je objavený ``alert_rule_roles`` Lookup, ktorý vracia len úlohy, ktoré sú skutočne zošrotované, takže fragment nemá svoj vlastný aktivačný stráž. Musí to začať na ``groups:`` úroveň položky."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Alert rules ship with the role.** `templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2` is discovered by the `alert_rule_roles` lookup, which returns only roles that are actually scraped, so the fragment carries no activation guard of its own. It must start at the `groups:` item level."
msgstr "**Výstražné pravidlá sú na lodi s úlohou.** `templates/prometheus/alert_rules.yml.j2` je objavený `alert_rule_roles` Lookup, ktorý vracia len úlohy, ktoré sú skutočne zošrotované, takže fragment nemá svoj vlastný aktivačný stráž. Musí to začať na `groups:` úroveň položky."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Alerting Support:** Works with the [`sys-ctl-alm-compose`](../sys-ctl-alm-compose/README.md) role for failure notifications."
