msgstr "**MCP Server:** Slúžiť štyri iba na čítanie Baserow nástroje pre AI klientov prostredníctvom adaptéra sidecar, ktorý chráni pred natívnym SSE koncovým bodom."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With Home Assistant deployed, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. Every discovered server is rendered into ``config.yaml`` under ``mcp_servers`` in the agent’s ``HERMES_HOME``, with the bearer referenced as ``${env:<ROLE>_MCP_TOKEN}`` so the config file carries no secret. The deploy then runs ``hermes mcp test`` per server and fails when one does not answer."
msgstr "**MCP klientská zmluva:** s Home Assistant nasadené, rola deklaruje MCP klientská strana zmluvy platformy ako interný streamable-HTTP klient s politikou iba na čítanie. Každý objavený server je prevedený do ``config.yaml`` pod ``mcp_servers`` v zastúpení ``HERMES_HOME``, s nositeľom referencie ako ``${env:<ROLE>_MCP_TOKEN}`` Takže konfiguračný súbor neobsahuje žiadne tajomstvo. Nasadenie potom beží ``hermes mcp test`` na server a zlyhá, keď človek neodpovedá."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With Home Assistant deployed, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. Every discovered server is rendered into `config.yaml` under `mcp_servers` in the agent's `HERMES_HOME`, with the bearer referenced as `${env:<ROLE>_MCP_TOKEN}` so the config file carries no secret. The deploy then runs `hermes mcp test` per server and fails when one does not answer."
