# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Paths that look wrong and are not.** Policies mount at `/openbao/policies/`, because OpenBao parses *every* file under `-config` as server configuration. Storage is `/openbao/file`, not `/openbao/data`: the image pre-chowns only `/openbao/{config,logs,file}` for the non-root `openbao` user, so a volume elsewhere lands root-owned and raft cannot write. `command:` is just `server` — the entrypoint appends `-config` itself, and passing it duplicates the flag."
msgstr "**Cesty, ktoré vyzerajú zle a nie sú.** Pripojiť politiky `/openbao/policies/`, pretože OpenBao parses *každých* súbor pod `-config` ako nastavenie servera. Skladovanie `/openbao/file`, nie `/openbao/data`: iba obrázok pred vytiahnutím `/openbao/{config,logs,file}` pre nekoreň `openbao` Užívateľ, takže objem inde pozemky koreňového vlastníctva a raft nemôže písať. `command:` je len `server` `-config` sama o sebe, a odovzdávanie duplikuje vlajku."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "**Paths that look wrong and are not.** Policies mount at ``/openbao/policies/``, because OpenBao parses *every* file under ``-config`` as server configuration. Storage is ``/openbao/file``, not ``/openbao/data``: the image pre-chowns only ``/openbao/{config,logs,file}`` for the non-root ``openbao`` user, so a volume elsewhere lands root-owned and raft cannot write. ``command:`` is just ``server`` — the entrypoint appends ``-config`` itself, and passing it duplicates the flag."
msgstr "**Cesty, ktoré vyzerajú zle a nie sú.** Pripojiť politiky ``/openbao/policies/``, pretože OpenBao parses *každých* súbor pod ``-config`` ako nastavenie servera. Skladovanie ``/openbao/file``, nie ``/openbao/data``: iba obrázok pred vytiahnutím ``/openbao/{config,logs,file}`` pre nekoreň ``openbao`` Užívateľ, takže objem inde pozemky koreňového vlastníctva a raft nemôže písať. ``command:`` je len ``server`` ``-config`` sama o sebe, a odovzdávanie duplikuje vlajku."

msgid "**Pause and resume:** ``app-control --config <file> stop|start <application_id>|all`` runs ``compose down`` and ``compose up -d`` in compose mode, and scales every service of the stack to 0 replicas or redeploys the rendered stack in swarm mode. The application’s own ``*.infinito.nexus`` timer stops and starts with it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Pause and resume:** `app-control --config <file> stop|start <application_id>|all` runs `compose down` and `compose up -d` in compose mode, and scales every service of the stack to 0 replicas or redeploys the rendered stack in swarm mode. The application's own `*.infinito.nexus` timer stops and starts with it."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused page.** While an application is paused, nginx answers every one of its vhosts with HTTP 503 and a page that shows an animation of a beaver sleeping behind a pause sign, states that the service is paused, and lists the platform operator's contact channels from `service_provider.contact` (email, Mastodon and the others declared there). The page text is multilingual and managed through the `core` `.po` catalogs."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused page:** While an application is paused, nginx answers every one of its vhosts with HTTP 503 and a self-contained page with a beaver sleeping behind a pause sign, the paused notice and the contact channels of ``service_provider.contact``. The page is rendered from the ``core`` gettext catalogs in every language they translate, picked from ``Accept-Language``, with English as the fallback."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Paused page:** While an application is paused, nginx answers every one of its vhosts with HTTP 503 and a self-contained page with a beaver sleeping behind a pause sign, the paused notice and the contact channels of `service_provider.contact`. The page is rendered from the `core` gettext catalogs in every language they translate, picked from `Accept-Language`, with English as the fallback."
