# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Restore verified against real dumps.** The *recover* CLI replays a generation's database and cluster dumps, reads the generation's own layout instead of guessing it, and places each dump by the engine the backup observed rather than by name alone. The *svc-bkp-volume-2-local* drill now empties every volume it claims to test, fails on a database that was never dumped, and stops the backup timers before it goes destructive. Baudolo is pinned per host, its contract read from baudolo itself."
msgstr "**Obnoviť overené proti skutočné skládky.** EÚ *zotavenie* CLI prehráva databázu generácie a kazetové skládky, číta vlastné rozloženie generácie namiesto hádania, a umiestni každý skládka podľa motora záložný skôr ako menom sám. EÚ *svc-bkp-volume-2-local* vŕtať teraz vyprázdňuje každý objem, o ktorom tvrdí, že testuje, zlyhá v databáze, ktorá nebola nikdy vyhodená, a zastaví záložné časovače pred tým, než to pôjde deštruktívne. Baudolo je prišpendovaný na hostiteľa, jeho zmluva je čítaná zo samotného baudola."

msgid "**Restricted SSO access:** With SSO enabled, ``security.oidc.auto_create_users`` stays off and `files/sql/rbac_reconcile.sql <./files/sql/rbac_reconcile.sql>`__ provisions Listmonk accounts only for the ``web-app-listmonk`` ``administrator`` (Super Admin), ``manager`` and ``viewer`` members, matched by email. The ``manager`` and ``viewer`` user roles are created with their permission sets from ``LISTMONK_RBAC_ROLES``. Every other account of type ``user`` is disabled, API accounts stay untouched, and the platform administrator stays Super Admin. The script runs through ``psql`` in the database container as an RBAC hook of `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync <../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/>`__ at every deploy and on its timer, so a group change reaches Listmonk within one timer interval."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted SSO access:** With SSO enabled, `security.oidc.auto_create_users` stays off and [files/sql/rbac_reconcile.sql](./files/sql/rbac_reconcile.sql) provisions Listmonk accounts only for the `web-app-listmonk` `administrator` (Super Admin), `manager` and `viewer` members, matched by email. The `manager` and `viewer` user roles are created with their permission sets from `LISTMONK_RBAC_ROLES`. Every other account of type `user` is disabled, API accounts stay untouched, and the platform administrator stays Super Admin. The script runs through `psql` in the database container as an RBAC hook of [sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync](../sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync/) at every deploy and on its timer, so a group change reaches Listmonk within one timer interval."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted Semaphore account:** the ``app-control`` user signs in only with the public half of the ``app_control_ssh_key`` credential of ``web-app-semaphore``. A forced command accepts ``app-control stop|start <application_id>|all`` and nothing else, and sudo lets the account run exactly those two subcommands as root."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted Semaphore account:** the `app-control` user signs in only with the public half of the `app_control_ssh_key` credential of `web-app-semaphore`. A forced command accepts `app-control stop|start <application_id>|all` and nothing else, and sudo lets the account run exactly those two subcommands as root."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted access:** The oauth2-proxy admits only members of the ``administrator`` and ``user`` role groups (``sso.oauth2.allowed_groups`` in ``meta/services.yml``). The LDAP filter of Snipe-IT admits the same two groups and leaves out the bootstrap administrator, which keeps its local password."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted access:** The oauth2-proxy admits only members of the ``administrator`` and ``user`` role groups."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted access:** The oauth2-proxy admits only members of the `administrator` and `user` role groups (`sso.oauth2.allowed_groups` in `meta/services.yml`). The LDAP filter of Snipe-IT admits the same two groups and leaves out the bootstrap administrator, which keeps its local password."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted access:** The oauth2-proxy admits only members of the `administrator` and `user` role groups."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted access:** ``sso.oauth2.allowed_groups`` in ``meta/services.yml`` admits only members of the ``web-app-n8n`` ``administrator`` and ``mcp`` RBAC groups. Every other Keycloak user, biber included, is refused by oauth2-proxy with a 403. n8n Community Edition offers no group-to-role mapping, so every admitted user except the owner (``users.administrator.email``) is provisioned as ``global:member``."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted access:** `sso.oauth2.allowed_groups` in `meta/services.yml` admits only members of the `web-app-n8n` `administrator` and `mcp` RBAC groups. Every other Keycloak user, biber included, is refused by oauth2-proxy with a 403. n8n Community Edition offers no group-to-role mapping, so every admitted user except the owner (`users.administrator.email`) is provisioned as `global:member`."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Restricted engine access:** The broker reaches the container engine only through a filtered unix socket in a volume shared with the socket proxy, which publishes no port and runs with ``network_mode: none`` in compose. The proxy admits only the container, service, task, network, volume and image calls the broker makes, and refuses every other method and path, including exec and delete. It filters methods and paths, not request bodies: ``volumes/create`` stays open for the per-agent volume, so the isolation holds against a compromised agent, which reaches no socket at all, not against a compromised broker."
msgstr "**Obmedzený prístup motora:** Sprostredkovateľ dosiahne kontajnerový motor iba cez filtrované Unix soketu vo zväzku zdieľaný so zásuvkovým proxy, ktorý neuverejňuje žiadny port a beží s ``network_mode: none`` v kompozícii. Proxy prijíma iba kontajner, službu, úlohu, sieť, objem a obraz volá makléra, a odmieta všetky ostatné metódy a cesty, vrátane exec a odstrániť. Filtruje metódy a cesty, nežiada orgány: ``volumes/create`` zostáva otvorený pre objem per-agent, takže izolácia drží proti kompromitovaného agenta, ktorý nedosiahne žiadnu zásuvku vôbec, nie proti kompromitovaného makléra."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Restricted engine access:** The broker reaches the container engine only through a filtered unix socket in a volume shared with the socket proxy, which publishes no port and runs with `network_mode: none` in compose. The proxy admits only the container, service, task, network, volume and image calls the broker makes, and refuses every other method and path, including exec and delete. It filters methods and paths, not request bodies: `volumes/create` stays open for the per-agent volume, so the isolation holds against a compromised agent, which reaches no socket at all, not against a compromised broker."
msgstr "**Obmedzený prístup motora:** Sprostredkovateľ dosiahne kontajnerový motor iba cez filtrované Unix soketu vo zväzku zdieľaný so zásuvkovým proxy, ktorý neuverejňuje žiadny port a beží s `network_mode: none` v kompozícii. Proxy prijíma iba kontajner, službu, úlohu, sieť, objem a obraz volá makléra, a odmieta všetky ostatné metódy a cesty, vrátane exec a odstrániť. Filtruje metódy a cesty, nežiada orgány: `volumes/create` zostáva otvorený pre objem per-agent, takže izolácia drží proti kompromitovaného agenta, ktorý nedosiahne žiadnu zásuvku vôbec, nie proti kompromitovaného makléra."

msgid "**Restricted project:** ``agents-<instance>`` allows unprivileged instances only, pool-managed disks only (no host path), managed network cards on the agent bridge only and no low-level VM options."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted project:** `agents-<instance>` allows unprivileged instances only, pool-managed disks only (no host path), managed network cards on the agent bridge only and no low-level VM options."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted sign-in:** Only members of the ``administrator`` and ``user`` role groups pass the oauth2-proxy gate (``sso.oauth2.allowed_groups``) and the LDAP ``filter_string`` of the auth source."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted sign-in:** Only members of the `administrator` and `user` role groups pass the oauth2-proxy gate (`sso.oauth2.allowed_groups`) and the LDAP `filter_string` of the auth source."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted sign-in:** With SSO, the gateway sets ``general_settings.ui_access_mode`` to ``restricted_sso_group`` on the ``web-app-litellm`` administrator group path in the groups claim, so the SSO login refuses every other Keycloak account with ``403`` before LiteLLM stores a user row; a refused login takes none of the five free SSO seats."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Restricted sign-in:** With SSO, the gateway sets `general_settings.ui_access_mode` to `restricted_sso_group` on the `web-app-litellm` administrator group path in the groups claim, so the SSO login refuses every other Keycloak account with `403` before LiteLLM stores a user row; a refused login takes none of the five free SSO seats."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retention and redaction.** Retention is an inventory parameter per log class with a default of 7 days. Secrets are redacted at the source where an application emits them and again in a central pipeline stage; a canary test proves that a synthetic secret never reaches Loki. The 200-line log excerpt that `sys-ctl-hlth-container` sends with its alerts is redacted by the same rules."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retention per log class:** ``services.loki.retention`` maps each log class the collector assigns (``access``, ``application``, ``system``, ``security``) to a duration (``<n>h``, ``<n>d`` or ``<n>w``, at least ``24h``), 7 days by default. The ``loki_retention`` filter turns the map into one ``retention_stream`` per class; the compactor deletes older lines."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retention per log class:** `services.loki.retention` maps each log class the collector assigns (`access`, `application`, `system`, `security`) to a duration (`<n>h`, `<n>d` or `<n>w`, at least `24h`), 7 days by default. The `loki_retention` filter turns the map into one `retention_stream` per class; the compactor deletes older lines."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retention:** Finished, failed and cancelled renders are removed after a configurable number of days."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retired Units:** The weekly hard repair, which ran ``compose down`` and ``up -d`` on every instance, is gone. Each host that still carries its timer, service or script stops, disables and deletes them on its next deploy, before the destructor unlocks the timers again. ``sys-ctl-rpr-container-soft`` restarts a project with an unhealthy or exited container instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Retired Units:** The weekly hard repair, which ran `compose down` and `up -d` on every instance, is gone. Each host that still carries its timer, service or script stops, disables and deletes them on its next deploy, before the destructor unlocks the timers again. `sys-ctl-rpr-container-soft` restarts a project with an unhealthy or exited container instead."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Retry-with-backoff:** transient SSH/rsync failures retry up to twelve times across a long window before surfacing as a hard failure."
msgstr "**Pozadie:** prechodným zlyhaním SSH/synchronizácie sa až dvanásťkrát prehrabáva cez dlhé okno predtým, ako sa objaví ako ťažká porucha."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reusable Role:** Can be used as a foundational component for software development, CI/CD pipelines, and build environments."
msgstr "**Opätovne použiteľná úloha:** Môže byť použitý ako základný komponent pre vývoj softvéru, CI/CD potrubia, a stavať prostredia."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reusable dependency role** for higher-level SSH workflows"
msgstr "**Úloha opakovanej závislosti** pre pracovné postupy SSH vyššej úrovne"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Revalidation required:** [ADR 0003 - One MCP surface per provider, and a disposition for every role](../architecture/decisions/0003-mcp-surface-per-provider.md) holds the exhaustive per-role audit and the standing contract, and supersedes this document where this document assumes an empty baseline, treats metadata as enforcement, or marks client provisioning and end-to-end authorization complete. The remaining work is tracked in [035 - MCP Proxy Expansion and Application Interconnection](035-mcp-proxy-expansion.md). Checked items below describe the original implementation slice and MUST NOT be read as proof that the stricter identity, revocation, transport, restart, proxy, and real-tool-call criteria in requirement 035 are complete."
msgstr "**Požadované predĺženie platnosti:** [ADR 0003 - Jeden MCP povrch na poskytovateľa, a dispozícia pre každú úlohu](../architecture/decisions/0003-mcp-surface-per-provider.md) je držiteľom úplného auditu na mieste a stálej zmluvy a nahrádza tento dokument, ak tento dokument predpokladá prázdnu východiskovú hodnotu, metaúdaje považuje za vynucovanie, alebo označuje klientske poskytovanie a ukončenie povolenia. Zostávajúca práca sa sleduje [035 - MCP Proxy Expanzia a prepojenie aplikácií](035-mcp-proxy-expansion.md). Kontrolované položky nižšie popisujú pôvodný implementačný plát a NESMIE sa čítať ako dôkaz toho, že prísnejšie identity, zrušenie, doprava, reštart, proxy, a real-tool-call kritériá v požiadavke 035 sú kompletné."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse Proxy**"
msgstr "**Reverzné proxy**"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Reverse Proxy**   Includes the `sys-stk-front-proxy` role to configure a proxy (e.g. NGINX) for routing HTTP(S) traffic to your database UI or management endpoint."
