msgstr ""

msgid "A ``container`` hook pipes its script into a command inside the application’s container, for applications whose image ships a scripting runtime. A ``host`` hook runs its script with the node’s Python beside its modules and reaches the container through ``$RBAC_SYNC_CONTAINER_BIN exec ... $RBAC_SYNC_CID``, for applications that only expose a CLI or an HTTP API inside the container. A hook runs on the node of the one container it names and reaches nothing else: in swarm no ``ports.local`` port is published, so an application whose hook acts on its database cannot also call its own HTTP API from there. Such work runs at deploy time inside the application’s network namespace, as `web-app-peertube <../web-app-peertube/README.md>`__ creates its accounts, and the hook keeps the SQL."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A ``database = '*'`` row dumps a whole instance with ``pg_dumpall``. It goes back through ``baudolo-restore cluster`` with the instance's superuser; its ``\\connect`` lines name the databases, while the consumers sit in the compose project of the engine, so both are checked."
msgstr "A ``database = '*'`` riadok skládky celú inštanciu s ``pg_dumpall``. Vracia sa späť. ``baudolo-restore cluster`` so superužívateľom inštancie; ``\\connect`` riadky označujú databázy, zatiaľ čo spotrebitelia sedia v kompozícii projektu motora, takže sa kontrolujú obe."

