msgid "A higher-level orchestration wrapper, *sys-stk-front-proxy* ties together several lower-level roles:"
msgstr "Vyšší orchester, *sys-stk-front-proxy* spája niekoľko úloh na nižšej úrovni:"

msgid "A host deployed with its own vault password takes `--host-vault-password-file <host>=<file>`, so its private key opens there."
msgstr ""

msgid "A host deployed with its own vault password takes ``--host-vault-password-file <host>=<file>``, so its private key opens there."
msgstr ""

msgid "A host may be a spoke of several meshes: it routes the pool through its first declared one and only the mesh subnet through the others, so no two interfaces claim one route."
msgstr ""

msgid "A host overrides one role in the inventory at `applications.<role>.services.<entity>.debug.enabled`, which wins over `meta/services.yml`. An override for a switch whose lookup the role never calls is dead config and fails the lint. [test_role_mode_switches.py](../../../../../tests/lint/ansible/variables/test_role_mode_switches.py) enforces the rule, and the lookups live in [debug.py](../../../../../plugins/lookup/debug.py) and [validate.py](../../../../../plugins/lookup/validate.py)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A host that cannot serve it"
msgstr "Hostiteľ, ktorý mu nemôže slúžiť"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A host that cannot serve the assigned kind"
msgstr "Hostiteľ, ktorý nemôže slúžiť pridelenému druhu"

msgid "A host whose ``svc-ai-litellm`` names a gateway host in ``services.litellm.gateway_host`` reaches that gateway over the mesh and runs none of its own. Provisioning it like any other host would put ``svc-ai-litellm`` into its inventory and mint a master key nothing uses, so the role is dropped before credentials are generated."
msgstr ""

msgid "A host with no previous environment file captures nothing and goes straight to the bootstrap path, which is the first deploy."
msgstr ""

msgid "A host without Mailu's maildir volume gets a note that there is nothing to import. Otherwise the deploy starts the import as the transient unit `stalwart-mailu-import` and moves on; a deploy that finds the unit still running leaves it alone. Follow it with `journalctl -fu stalwart-mailu-import`: it logs `[PROGRESS]` every 1000 messages of a folder, one `[MAILBOX] <mailbox> -> <account>: found=<n> imported=<n> skipped=<n> failed=<n> sieve=<state>` line per mailbox, one line per folder below it, `[SKIP]` for every mailbox outside the served domains, a closing `[SUMMARY]` and `[DONE] rc=<n>`. When the unit stops, it removes the staged credentials. An import that ends with `[DONE] rc=0` leaves the marker `.mailu-import.done` in the Stalwart instance directory, and no later deploy starts the import again while it exists; delete the marker to import again. A failed import leaves no marker, so the next deploy repeats it, and the repeat imports nothing twice: a message is skipped when its Message-ID, or without one its Date/From/To/Subject, is already in the target folder, and a Sieve script with unchanged content is left alone. Turn the switch off once Mailu is retired."
msgstr ""

msgid "A host without Mailu’s maildir volume gets a note that there is nothing to import. Otherwise the deploy starts the import as the transient unit ``stalwart-mailu-import`` and moves on; a deploy that finds the unit still running leaves it alone. Follow it with ``journalctl -fu stalwart-mailu-import``: it logs ``[PROGRESS]`` every 1000 messages of a folder, one ``[MAILBOX] <mailbox> -> <account>: found=<n> imported=<n> skipped=<n> failed=<n> sieve=<state>`` line per mailbox, one line per folder below it, ``[SKIP]`` for every mailbox outside the served domains, a closing ``[SUMMARY]`` and ``[DONE] rc=<n>``. When the unit stops, it removes the staged credentials. An import that ends with ``[DONE] rc=0`` leaves the marker ``.mailu-import.done`` in the Stalwart instance directory, and no later deploy starts the import again while it exists; delete the marker to import again. A failed import leaves no marker, so the next deploy repeats it, and the repeat imports nothing twice: a message is skipped when its Message-ID, or without one its Date/From/To/Subject, is already in the target folder, and a Sieve script with unchanged content is left alone. Turn the switch off once Mailu is retired."
msgstr ""

msgid "A host-mode-only provider such as svc-bkp-volume-2-local never gets a swarm row, so a swarm iteration on it deploys it inside another row's closure. Every row whose include set carries the provider qualifies, but those sets differ by more than an order of magnitude in what they pull. The rows are ranked by the summed ``min_storage`` of the include set the provision step derives, then by the complexity ``weight``, then by token, so the lightest host comes first."
msgstr ""

msgid "A host-mode-only role has no swarm row; deploy it inside the lightest host row \\`python -m cli.meta.ci.host\\_rows --provides <service key> --mode swarm\\` ranks first."
msgstr ""

msgid "A host-name entry covers the name and every name below it, so `example.org` and `*.example.org` are the same entry. dnsmasq matches on label boundaries and has no form for one host without its subdomains, so an exact-host meaning would promise something the resolver cannot keep. Only one leading `*.` is accepted. A CIDR with host bits set is refused, not widened, and a name whose last label is all digits is refused as a mistyped address."
msgstr ""

msgid "A host-name entry covers the name and every name below it. dnsmasq, which carries the decision onto the wire, matches on label boundaries the same way and has no form for one host without its subdomains, so ``example.org`` and ``*.example.org`` are the same entry. A narrower meaning here would promise an exactness the resolver cannot keep."
msgstr ""

msgid "A hosted runner that fills its disk, exhausts its RAM or wedges on a stuck mount dies without a trace: the Actions Worker stops, the deploy step stays ``in_progress`` and every diagnostic upload after it stays ``pending``, so no artifact survives. The watchdog samples the host while the step runs and ends the step itself once a floor is crossed, which turns a silent job loss into a failed step the post-mortem and upload steps still get to run after."
msgstr ""

msgid "A hub named in the inventory for Compose deployments, with roaming spokes that dial it with `PersistentKeepalive` and are never waited for."
msgstr ""

msgid "A hub named in the inventory for Compose deployments, with roaming spokes that dial it with ``PersistentKeepalive`` and are never waited for."
msgstr ""

msgid "A human developer reconfigures any role the way applications are reconfigured: the inventory's `agents.<role>` is deep-merged over the role's `agent.yml` and `cron.yml`, and every consumer reads the merged result through one lookup (`lookup('agent_config', role, path)`), never the raw files."
msgstr ""

msgid "A human of the longest form still gets a Bluesky handle with the `kc-` prefix. Superseded by the handle rules of the `web-app-bluesky` login broker (`files/login-broker/`): a short username keeps its name as the handle, a reserved one gets the `i8-` prefix, a username over 18 characters picks its handle in a form, and a legacy `kc-` account is reported."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A jeff that cannot be reached rejects the request. It is not routed around, because the caller named an alias precisely so it would not have to know which model answered, and substituting a different decider would make that answer mean something else."
msgstr "Jeff, ktorý nemôže byť prijatý, zamietne žiadosť. Nie je routed okolo, pretože volajúci pomenoval prezývku presne tak, aby nemusel vedieť, ktorý model odpovedal, a nahradenie iný rozhodner by túto odpoveď znamenať niečo iné."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A job URL narrows the download to that job's app; a bare run URL pulls every `role-runtimes-*` artifact in the run."
msgstr "URL úlohy zužuje sťahovanie aplikácie tejto úlohy; holé spustenie URL ťahá každý `role-runtimes-*` artefakt na úteku."

# gained=['"aktuálne"']
# dokončená, keď modul nahlásil ``failed``, alebo keď príkaz vrátil non-nula
# ``rc``. Čo odlišuje skutočné zlyhanie od bezvýznamného no-op sa líši podľa
# API a žije v rôznych kľúčoch: moduly dať do ``msg`` (odpovede na cloudflare
# "Rovnaký záznam už existuje"), príkazy dať do ``stdout`` (``ollama pull``
# odtlačky "aktuálne" a východy nenulové). Oba sú prehľadané, takže volajúci
# prechádza tolerované frázovanie a nemusí vedieť, ktorý kľúč ho nesie.
msgid "A job counts as failed when it never finished, when the module reported ``failed``, or when a command returned a non-zero ``rc``. What distinguishes a real failure from an idempotent no-op differs per API and lives in different keys: modules put it in ``msg`` (cloudflare answers \"An identical record already exists\"), commands put it in ``stdout`` (``ollama pull`` prints \"up to date\" and exits non-zero). Both are searched, so a caller passes the tolerated phrasing and does not have to know which key carries it."
msgstr ""

msgid "A job submitted while every runner is busy or held waits in the queue and prints its position. An optional `timeout=` makes make give up loudly; by default there is no timeout."
msgstr ""

msgid "A job that never finished always counts as transient: a hung request, or a job that died before its module ran and left its job file at \"started\". Any other failure is transient only when what it said matches ``transient``."
msgstr ""

msgid "A job that runs after a failed `needs` guards its `if:` with `!cancelled()`, not `always()`, so a cancel stops it. Only `done` and `report-main-failures` keep `always()`: they report the cancelled run. Enforced by [test_workflow_cancellable_jobs_no_always.py](../../tests/lint/repository/test_workflow_cancellable_jobs_no_always.py)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A job title states its whole combination, which lets `--failed` replay the mode, onion state and distribution, and makes a plan table row comparable to the job it predicts."
msgstr "Názov pracovného miesta uvádza celú jeho kombináciu, ktorá umožňuje `--failed` prehrať režim, stav cibule a distribúcia, a robí riadok tabuľky plánu porovnateľné s úlohou, ktorú predpovedá."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A job's green conclusion is **NOT** evidence for a specific change. Before citing a run as proof, you MUST locate the line in that job's log where the change executed: a Playwright spec's `✓` (a leading `-` means the spec was skipped), the env var inside the container, or the command text of an `if:`-gated step. If the string is absent, report the run as silent on the change, not as supporting it."
msgstr "Zelený záver práce je **NIE** dôkaz o konkrétnej zmene. Pred citovaním beh ako dôkaz, musíte nájsť riadok v zázname práce, kde zmena vykonaná: Playwright Spec je `✓` (vedenie `-` To znamená, že spec bol preskočený.), env var vnútri kontajnera, alebo príkaz text `if:`-Prepustený krok. Ak reťazec chýba, nahláste spustenie ako tiché o zmene, nie ako podpora."

msgid "A key counts as read when core declares it in ``group_vars`` or a role's ``defaults`` or ``vars``, tests it with ``is defined`` or ``| default(`` in its YAML or Jinja, reads it by name from the variables in a plugin, is one of the ``SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>`` names the email lookup builds at run time, or is a record the provisioning CLI keeps in host_vars and reads back on its next run."
msgstr ""

msgid "A key set in the role's own ``services.design`` entry wins over the ``web-svc-design`` value; ``false``/``0`` disables the replacement for that scope, and a ``true`` title resolves to the role README H1."
msgstr ""

msgid "A key that resolves to none of them, an empty list, or a value that is no JSON list of names makes the plugin raise and name the variable or the key. `keycloak_managed` stays guarded whatever the list holds."
msgstr ""

msgid "A key that some environment declares per run therefore MUST be written by a dedicated handler through `eb.set`. The exporting shell still wins for its own run, because [load.sh](../../scripts/meta/env/load.sh) preserves non-empty caller values when it sources `.env`; the file keeps the derived default. `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB`, `INFINITO_CACHE_STACK` and `INFINITO_GHCR_MIRROR` are written this way. Note the consequence: for those keys `.env` and the running shell can legitimately disagree, and `.env` is not the authority."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A key's comment is the most recent contiguous block of `# ...` lines directly above the `KEY=...` line, joined with single spaces. Section headers (`# --- ... ---`) are treated as separators: they reset the pending comment so the next key starts fresh, instead of inheriting the heading line as its own documentation."
msgstr "Komentár kľúča je posledný susediaci blok `# ...` priamo nad čiarami `KEY=...` čiara spojená s jedným priestorom. Hlavičky tried (`# --- ... ---`) sú považované za separátory: resetujú čakajúci komentár, takže ďalší kľúč začne nový, namiesto toho, aby zdedil smer ako vlastnú dokumentáciu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A label that silently stops resolving to arm64 turns the whole axis into a green lie."
msgstr ""

msgid "A language pull request is opened only after its verification passed: every entry filled and not fuzzy, `msgfmt --check` clean, placeholders and protected spans identical to the source, glossary terms kept, and a sampled quality judgement by the chat judge (`utils/i18n/judge.py`, a chat model through `svc-ai-litellm`, three written-out levels, `temperature: 0`) at or above the language's last accepted level. A judge reply without a level aborts the verification instead of scoring."
msgstr ""

msgid "A legacy domain that only receives mail is declared under ``services.stalwart.alias_domains``; ``<local>@<source>`` is then delivered to ``<local>@<target>``:"
msgstr ""

