msgid "A pin is in force only while the role carrying it is part of the round's include and runs the variant the marker stands in. A pin in a role the round does not deploy changes nothing. The round starts every role on its clamped index and recomputes the include and the pins in force until the assignment no longer changes; pins that never settle raise `VariantPinError`. [test_variant_pin_fixed_point.py](../../../../../tests/integration/roles/meta/variants/test_variant_pin_fixed_point.py) settles every round the matrix plans (each role as the only primary, in each of its variants) and fails when a round raises `VariantPinError`, or when a pin in force stands above a service entry the carrier runs with `enabled: false` in that round. Place a pin only above an entry the variant keeps enabled: the guide host `docs` stays on for the primary app alone, so a pin above `docs` fails the guard in any round that pulls the role in as a dependency running that variant."
