msgid "Baserow's native `openid_connect` auth provider belongs to the bundled enterprise plugin and refuses to register without a paid Baserow Enterprise licence, so the addon ships declared and off and the oauth2-proxy front door above stays the supported SSO path. An operator holding that licence switches the addon on; [files/playwright/addons/openid_connect.spec.js](./files/playwright/addons/openid_connect.spec.js) then asserts the provider is registered and offered on the login page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Baserow's web frontend sends every API call to its one `PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL` and marks its `jwt_token` cookie `Secure` from its one public URL, so a session cannot live on the onion sibling. `meta/networks.yml` therefore opts into `reachability.handover`: the onion vhost in [proxy.conf.j2](templates/proxy.conf.j2) answers `/` with a redirect to the same path on the canonical clearnet URL."
msgstr ""

