msgid "Home Assistant is the open-source home-automation platform. It ships a **native Model Context Protocol Server integration** ([`mcp_server`](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/mcp_server/)) that implements Streamable HTTP and exposes Home Assistant's Assist API to MCP clients, with per-entity access control (only explicitly exposed entities are reachable). It can control lights, climate, covers, switches, sensors, media players, fans, locks, vacuums, and cameras."
msgstr "Home Assistant je open-source domácej automatizácie platformy. To loďou **Name** ([`mcp_server`](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/mcp_server/)) ktorá implementuje HTTP a odhalí Home Assistant's Assist API pre klientov MCP, ktorí majú kontrolu prístupu podľa jednotlivých subjektov (len explicitne exponované subjekty sú dosiahnuteľné)Môže ovládať svetlá, podnebie, kryty, prepínače, senzory, prehrávače médií, ventilátory, zámky, vysávače a kamery."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Home Assistant ships the MCP server as a native integration. The role enables it through ``mcp.enabled``, which stays true only while an MCP client role is part of the deployment."
