msgid "The RBAC sync changes only accounts the directory owns: the members of the three role groups and every account a `User Social Login` row links to the directory, either the `keycloak` row Frappe writes at a Keycloak sign-in (`ERPNEXT_SSO_PROVIDER_NAME`) or the `directory` row the sync writes on every member it converges (`ERPNEXT_RBAC_DIRECTORY_PROVIDER_NAME`). On such an account outside every role group it revokes only the roles of `ERPNEXT_RBAC_ROLE_GRANTS` and disables the account only when no other role remains, so a role a consumer granted keeps it enabled. The Keycloak sign-in applies the same rule to the account that signs in. Service, API, website and customer accounts a consumer created outside the directory keep their roles and stay enabled."
