msgid "The file's pre-``%changelog`` head is preserved verbatim. The ``%changelog`` section is replaced with one stanza per entry plus the trailing notice. Returns ``True`` when the file was rewritten, ``False`` when nothing happened (missing file, no ``%changelog`` section, no entries, or dry run)."
msgstr "Spis je pred-``%changelog`` hlava je zachovaná doslovne. EÚ ``%changelog`` sekcia je nahradená jednou stanzou na jeden záznam a zároveň aj oznamom. Description ``True`` keď bol súbor prepísaný, ``False`` keď sa nič nestalo (Chýbajúci súbor, nie ``%changelog`` sekcia, žiadne vstupy, alebo suchý beh)."

msgid "The file-based job queue: submit, claim by one idle runner under a lock, the states `queued`, `running`, `held`, `done` and `failed`, hold and release, the queue position, the wait with an optional timeout that withdraws the job, the log follow that returns the job's exit status, and the cleanup report of held jobs and job stacks without a record."
msgstr ""

msgid "The filer page runs its own inline script (it defines `reportProgress` for the upload progress bar) and inline event handlers, but `meta/csp.yml` grants neither `script-src-elem` nor `script-src-attr`. They run only because `build_csp_header` (`plugins/filter/csp_filters.py`) adds `'unsafe-inline'` to both directives whenever the `logout` service is enabled. With `logout` disabled the browser refuses them (\"Executing inline script violates ... script-src-elem\", \"Executing inline event handler violates ... script-src-attr\"), the upload progress never renders, and the design spec \"the upload progress bar is the primary fill and carries its on-color\" fails. Options: grant the filer's script needs in `meta/csp.yml` (flags for both directives, or hashes of the upstream snippets per pinned version), or let the filer page carry its own policy."
msgstr ""

