msgid "The maintained native path needs Kibana Agent Builder with its index privileges and licence; the older sidecar is deprecated."
msgstr "Udržiavaná rodná cesta potrebuje Kibana Agent Builder s jeho index oprávnenia a preukaz; starší postranný vozík je deprekovaný."

msgid "The maintainer may start work without the `Approved` gate only on failed runs of the own repository's CI and on security alerts. Issues from non-collaborators and fork pull request runs go through the planner and the gate."
msgstr ""

msgid "The major version prefixed with ``v``, as the release schedule keys it."
msgstr ""

msgid "The make command each planned row runs."
msgstr ""

msgid "The make exit code is never a verdict, because the log pipe hides it. A quality-high whose test phase is red never runs its lint phase, so a run that looks like two failed targets may have skipped every lint target."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The make target ultimately calls the same CLI, so any behaviour described here applies to both."
msgstr "Make cieľ nakoniec nazýva rovnaké CLI, takže akékoľvek správanie tu popísané platí pre oboch."

msgid "The managed block: one table of header-trust roles, one of exempted files."
msgstr ""

msgid "The managed block: the legend and the Mermaid flowchart."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The manager legs of steps 2, 4 and 9 run only when the app's include closure contains `svc-bkp-volume-2-local` / `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`. `utils/tests/swarm/backup_repos.py` derives both the manager's inventory groups and the `remote-2-local` provider list from that closure; apps without those roles prove the chain through the nfs repository."
msgstr "Vedúci úseky schodov 2, 4 a 9 spustiť iba vtedy, ak aplikácia obsahuje uzavretie `svc-bkp-volume-2-local` / `svc-bkp-secrets-2-local`. `utils/tests/swarm/backup_repos.py` Description `remote-2-local` zoznam poskytovateľov z tohto uzavretia; aplikácie bez týchto úloh dokazujú reťazec prostredníctvom úložiska nfs."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The manifest document, or None when the generation carries none."
msgstr "Zjavný dokument, alebo žiadny, keď generácia nemá žiadne."

msgid "The manifest names a config blob and the blob carries the sections a ``Dockerfile`` baked in. Reading one section is the same walk as reading another, so both callers share it: resolve the index to a platform, read the blob, take the section."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The manual entry workflow (`entry-manual-steer.yml`) sets `cancel-in-progress: true` on its own group, and the orchestrator's group cancels for `workflow_dispatch` regardless of ref, so a manual sweep supersedes on both levels, `main` included."
msgstr "Manuálny vstup (`entry-manual-steer.yml`) sady `cancel-in-progress: true` vo vlastnej skupine a orchestrálna skupina ruší `workflow_dispatch` bez ohľadu na ref, takže manuálne zametanie nahrádza na oboch úrovniach, `main` zahrnuté."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The map itself is generated, never tracked, so no second copy of a hostname can drift; ``utils.cache.render.render_artifacts`` writes it once the value-set is built."
msgstr "Samotná mapa je generovaná, nikdy nesledovaná, takže žiadna druhá kópia mena hostiteľa nemôže unášať; ``utils.cache.render.render_artifacts`` píše ju akonáhle je hodnota-set je postavený."

msgid "The map of which role wires in which is derived from the roles themselves on every docs build, by [infinito_docs/generators/integrations.py](../../roles/web-app-docs/files/python/infinito_docs/generators/integrations.py), and reached from [docs/architecture/integrations.rst](../architecture/integrations.rst). Its two sources are the declarations this requirement governs: a **wired** edge comes from a top-level service key in the row role's `meta/services.yml`, and a **declared** edge from the `bridges:` entry of a `meta/addons/*.yml`. Edges are directional — the row hosts the flag or the plugin — so a bidirectional pair such as `nextcloud`↔`openproject` appears twice. It currently covers 98 roles with **811 wired edges plus 99 bridged addon edges**."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marked row carries `instructions: <mode>` in the matrix JSON, and the plan table names that mode in its 📖 column; its job title is that of an ordinary deploy row."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The marker adds `web-app-docs` to that row's `apps`, so the documentation is deployed beside the role under test. Its own CLI test then reads the role's page, takes the Production block out of the rendered HTML, and runs it."
msgstr "Značka pridáva `web-app-docs` do toho riadku `apps`, takže dokumentácia je nasadená mimo úlohu, ktorá je v teste. Jeho vlastný test CLI potom číta stránku role, berie výrobný blok z prevedenej HTML, a spustí ho."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The marker file carries the same name as the swarm drill's (`scripts/tests/deploy/swarm/routine/backup/base.sh`) — one name for one concept. The implementations stay apart on purpose: the swarm drill follows a single token across five hops on four machines from the controller, which has nothing in common with marking every subject of one host beyond the three lines that write a file and read it back."
msgstr "Súbor markerov má rovnaké meno ako vŕtačka roja. (`scripts/tests/deploy/swarm/routine/backup/base.sh`) Jeden názov pre jeden koncept. Implementácie zostávajú od seba naschvál: rojná vŕtačka nasleduje jeden token cez päť chmeľu na štyroch strojoch z regulátora, ktorý nemá nič spoločné s označením každého predmetu jedného hostiteľa za tri riadky, ktoré píšu súbor a čítať späť."

msgid "The marker is a comment, so it never reaches the merged services map or `host_vars`. It applies only to the variant entry it stands in; the same role's other variants are unaffected. A primary app keeps the index the sweep assigned it and no pin overrides it."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marker lives beside the pins that cause the overage, so it is visible to whoever edits them, and it is registered as a rule in [suppression.md](../../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md) like every other suppression. It expires on its own: `test_every_mem_limit_exemption_is_still_needed` fails once the marked variant fits again, so it cannot outlive the cause it was written for. Add one only when no variant placement brings the footprint under the cap, and record in the text which placements were tried."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marker lives outside the stack and its volumes, so it survives ``docker stack rm``, ``docker compose down``, a crashed database and the stop and start cycle of ``backup.project_hard_restart``. A host that carries the marker therefore redeploys while its dedicated database is down, as in the restore of ```svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`` <../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/README.md>`__ (``docker stack rm``, restore, redeploy). A dedicated store on a host without the marker, such as a 0.16 host or a host whose instance directory was lost, needs its database running before the deploy: start the database service of the stack the host last deployed, then deploy. Before a host that carries the marker goes back to a 0.16 store, through ``stalwart-migrate rollback`` or a backup taken under 0.16, delete the marker, so the next deploy reads the store."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marker lives outside the stack and its volumes, so it survives `docker stack rm`, `docker compose down`, a crashed database and the stop and start cycle of `backup.project_hard_restart`. A host that carries the marker therefore redeploys while its dedicated database is down, as in the restore of [`svc-bkp-nfs-2-local`](../svc-bkp-nfs-2-local/README.md) (`docker stack rm`, restore, redeploy). A dedicated store on a host without the marker, such as a 0.16 host or a host whose instance directory was lost, needs its database running before the deploy: start the database service of the stack the host last deployed, then deploy. Before a host that carries the marker goes back to a 0.16 store, through `stalwart-migrate rollback` or a backup taken under 0.16, delete the marker, so the next deploy reads the store."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marker names the directory it was placed as, so a copy of a placed role under another name, which carries the same file, never counts as placed. It is written and read without following a symbolic link."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "The marker sits on the construct's own line or on any line of the comment block directly above it, Jinja ``{# #}`` or ``#``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marker sits on the definition's line or in the comment block above it, and answers every read through that name and through the names derived from it."
msgstr ""

msgid "The marker that identifies a custom role the pull placed under ``roles/``."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The match stream is built once per process by `_scan.iter_matches` and shared across the four test classes; the repo-derived context (application defaults, user defaults, per-role schemas, `application_id`-declaring role set) comes from `_scan.get_context`. Validation helpers live in `_validate.py`. Suppression is wired through the project's `noqa` / `nocheck` grammar; the rule key is `lookup-config-path` (see [suppression.md](../../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md))."
msgstr "Match stream je postavený raz za proces `_scan.iter_matches` a delili sa o štyri testovacie triedy; kontext odvodený z repo obchodu (predvolené aplikácie, predvolené užívateľské nastavenia, schémy pre každý stupeň, `application_id`-vyhlasovací súbor úloh) pochádza z `_scan.get_context`. Validácia pomocníci žijú v `_validate.py`. Potlačenie je zapojené cez projekt `noqa` / `nocheck` gramatika; kľúčom k pravidlu je `lookup-config-path` (Pozri [suppression.md](../../../../../docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md))."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matcher itself lives in :mod:`utils.cache.gitignore` (single SPOT for ``.gitignore`` parsing and matching). :func:`iter_non_ignored_files` here composes the cached project walk with that matcher and is the recommended helper for lint tests that want the \"files git would track\" view without subprocessing."
msgstr "Zápalník sám žije v :mod:`utils.cache.gitignore` (jeden SPOT pre ``.gitignore`` spracovanie a vyrovnávanie). :func:`iter_non_ignored_files` tu komponuje cached projekt chôdze s týmto zápalníkom a je odporúčaný pomocník pre Lint testy, ktoré chcú \"súbory git by vystopovali\" pohľad bez podspracovania."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The materialised application payload exposes services under the bare ``services`` key (no ``compose.services`` wrapper). The function name is preserved for backwards compatibility with existing call sites."
msgstr "Zhmotnené využitie užitočného zaťaženia odhaľuje služby pod holým ``services`` kľúč (no ``compose.services`` obal). Názov funkcie je zachovaný pre spätnú kompatibilitu s existujúcimi miestami hovorov."

msgid "The matrix and survey backlog (the per-role upstream-plugin survey, wiring every open cell, gating integration addons on their partner, opt-in paid cells, reconciling already-wired plugins, the cross-role integration specs and the SSO cells) moved to the acceptance criteria of [027](027-integration-matrix.md)."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix hands every row exactly one filesystem, so the value a deploy job sees is always narrow. Reading that narrowness as a demand would turn every condition the applying step is built to tolerate into a red row: a loop device it could not claim, a pool another job still holds, a kernel without the module."
msgstr "Matica radí každý riadok presne jeden súborový systém, takže hodnota nasadenie práce vidí vždy úzky. Čítanie, že zúženie ako dopyt by premenila každú podmienku aplikačný krok je postavený tak, aby toleroval do červeného radu: slučka zariadenie, ktoré nemohol nárokovať, bazén ďalšiu prácu stále drží, jadro bez modulu."

msgid "The matrix orchestrator (`utils/tests/swarm/matrix.py`) drives the deploy stage per variant round; `routine/00_one.sh` drives the surrounding stages for one distro, and the workflow `.github/workflows/call-test-deploy.yml` drives the distro loop. Run one app locally with `make swarm-zombie app=<id>` or the whole matrix via `make roundtrip`. Both copy the rescue bundle to the host through `utils/release.sh` and then release the cluster; `keep=true` keeps it for inspection."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix orchestrator needs these before it provisions, so that the authorized_keys reach host_vars through the merging ``--vars`` channel rather than through the replacing extra-vars file."
msgstr "Matrice orchester potrebuje pred tým, než sa ustanovenia, takže authorized_keys dosah host_vars prostredníctvom zlúčenia ``--vars`` kanál skôr ako prostredníctvom náhradného extra-vars súboru."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The matrix-variant planner (see [variants.md](variants.md)) calls the expansion once per round, so each round's inventory gets the right transitive closure for that round's variant set."
msgstr "Matice-variantné plánovač (Pozri [variants.md](variants.md)) volá rozšírenie raz za kolo, takže každý kolo inventár dostane správne tranzitívne uzavretie pre to kolo variantu sada."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mautrix network bridges are declared in ``meta/addons/`` as ``mechanism: bridge`` addons (requirement 026, Decision 13). Each is ``required: false`` and **disabled by default**; its per-network DB password and its appservice ``as_token``/``hs_token`` pair are referenced from ```meta/secrets.yml`` <./meta/secrets.yml>`__ ``credentials:``, never inlined. The role renders each bridge’s ``config.yaml`` and the matching Synapse ``registration.yaml`` from the same tokens."
msgstr "Mautrix sieťové mosty sú deklarované v ``meta/addons/`` ako ``mechanism: bridge`` doplnky (požiadavka 026, rozhodnutie 13). Každý je ``required: false`` a **automaticky vypnuté**; jeho na sieť DB heslo a jeho appservice ``as_token``/``hs_token`` @ info: tooltip ```meta/secrets.yml`` <./meta/secrets.yml>`__ ``credentials:``, never inlined. The role renders each bridge’s ``config.yaml`` and the matching Synapse ``registration.yaml`` z rovnakého tokenu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mautrix network bridges are declared in `meta/addons/` as `mechanism: bridge` addons (requirement 026, Decision 13). Each is `required: false` and **disabled by default**; its per-network DB password and its appservice `as_token`/`hs_token` pair are referenced from [`meta/secrets.yml`](./meta/secrets.yml) `credentials:`, never inlined. The role renders each bridge's `config.yaml` and the matching Synapse `registration.yaml` from the same tokens."
msgstr "Mautrix sieťové mosty sú deklarované v `meta/addons/` ako `mechanism: bridge` doplnky (požiadavka 026, rozhodnutie 13). Každý je `required: false` a **automaticky vypnuté**; jeho na sieť DB heslo a jeho appservice `as_token`/`hs_token` @ info: tooltip [`meta/secrets.yml`](./meta/secrets.yml) `credentials:`, nikdy vložené. Úloha robí každý most `config.yaml` a zodpovedajúca Synapse `registration.yaml` z rovnakého tokenu."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The measurement decides **which** value each axis takes, never **whether** it takes one:"
msgstr "Meranie rozhodne **ktoré** hodnota každej osi nikdy **či** Po prvé:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The merged map is what the inventory ALSO bakes into host_vars, so feeding the same dict into `CombinedResolver(services_overrides=...)` eliminates the topology-vs-host_vars drift that variant-blind resolution produced."
msgstr "Zlúčená mapa je to, čo inventár ALS preniká do host_vars, takže kŕmenie rovnaký dict do `CombinedResolver(services_overrides=...)` eliminuje topológiu-vs-host_vars drift že variant-zaslepené rozlíšenie vyrobené."

msgid "The mesh is written by one cross-host pass before the play, never by the role:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The mesh must exist in the inventory before the play runs. Write it once over every inventory of the deploy, including any sibling file that holds hosts the cluster inventory does not:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The mesh state is replayed the same way, and as the boolean the title carried rather than only when it is true. These tokens feed the priority line, where an unpinned mesh axis offers both states: a failed direct swarm row came back as itself *and* as a meshed sibling, spending two jobs to reproduce one. The pin halves that to the arm that actually failed. Only a mode the mesh axis covers takes it, so a compose token stays as short as it was."
msgstr ""

msgid "The mesh states a priority row takes, global axis ahead of the pin."
msgstr ""

msgid "The meshes are inventory values, and every role ships them empty. ``networks.meshes`` of this role declares them in the hub’s ``host_vars``, or in the ``host_vars`` of every member when there is no hub, and ``networks.meshes`` of every other role lists the meshes its hosts join. A host that carries no other role on the mesh joins by listing the mesh name in this role’s own ``networks.meshes``; a mapping there declares a mesh, a name joins one. The development lab declares two, ``swarm`` and ``data``, in `wireguard.yml <../../inventories/development/wireguard.yml>`__; `wireguard-three-meshes <../../inventories/examples/wireguard-three-meshes/README.md>`__ declares three. Consumers read a host’s mesh address through ``lookup('mesh_address', <host>)`` instead of naming a mesh."
msgstr ""

msgid "The meshes are inventory values, and every role ships them empty. `networks.meshes` of this role declares them in the hub's `host_vars`, or in the `host_vars` of every member when there is no hub, and `networks.meshes` of every other role lists the meshes its hosts join. A host that carries no other role on the mesh joins by listing the mesh name in this role's own `networks.meshes`; a mapping there declares a mesh, a name joins one. The development lab declares two, `swarm` and `data`, in [wireguard.yml](../../inventories/development/wireguard.yml); [wireguard-three-meshes](../../inventories/examples/wireguard-three-meshes/README.md) declares three. Consumers read a host's mesh address through `lookup('mesh_address', <host>)` instead of naming a mesh."
msgstr ""

msgid "The meshes declared in *applications*, in declaration order."
msgstr ""

msgid "The meshes the deployment declares, in declaration order."
msgstr ""

msgid "The message is the fault element's ``message`` attribute, falling back to its text body; ``system_out`` is the testcase's ``<system-out>`` text."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The metrics endpoint needs a server-generated token that cannot be pre-seeded into a static scrape config from the inventory. Same pattern as `web-app-gitea`. Gives the `openbao_core_unsealed` gauge."
msgstr "Merný koncový ukazovateľ potrebuje server generovaný žetónom, ktorý nemožno vopred zasadiť do statického šrotu skonfiškovať z inventára. Rovnaký vzor ako `web-app-gitea`. Dáva `openbao_core_unsealed` mierka."

msgid "The migration (D2) is the first `make cache-evict` on a cache above its cap: it runs the same age and size eviction, so warm entries inside the cap stay and no cache directory is removed or recreated. `make clean-cache` keeps its wipe semantics and is never called by another target."
msgstr ""

msgid "The minimum env set for any spec following the persona flows is `APP_BASE_URL`, `CANONICAL_DOMAIN`, and `LOGOUT_URL`. `DASHBOARD_BASE_URL` is rendered only by the dashboard role's own spec, because consumer personas enter at `APP_BASE_URL` directly. Specs that gate on auth additionally read at least one of `OIDC_ISSUER_URL`, `KEYCLOAK_BASE_URL`, plus the persona credentials `ADMIN_USERNAME` / `ADMIN_PASSWORD` and `BIBER_USERNAME` / `BIBER_PASSWORD`. Specs that exercise integrations (Matomo, Discourse, Email, Prometheus, …) read the integration-specific keys defined in the [`playwright.env.j2` skill](../../../../../agents/skills/i8-file-role-playwright-env/SKILL.md)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The mirror of :func:`untranslated`, and the half that catches a model answering a language it cannot write with one it can: Chamorro came back in Han because the code ``ch`` reads as Chinese, Turkish in Bengali, Avestan in Arabic. A target that writes its own name in Latin letters has no business returning a line that carries almost none."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mirror workflow runs as stage 8 of the CI pipeline. See [ci.md](../git/pipeline.md). It runs in parallel with the DNS tests and MUST complete before deploy tests start."
msgstr "Zrkadlo workflow beží ako etapa 8 plynovodu CI. Pozri [ci.md](../git/pipeline.md). To beží paralelne s DNS testy a MUSÍ dokončiť pred nasadením skúšky začať."

# translated-by: libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The mirrors file is generated into the inventory directory. The inventory creator applies mirror image overrides to host variables via `cli/administration/inventory/provision/mirror_overrides.py`, which reads `mirrors.yml.applications` and writes `applications.{role}.services.{service}.image` (and `.version`) into host vars subject to the per-service `mirror_policy`."
msgstr "Súbor zrkadiel sa vygeneruje do inventára. Tvorca inventáru používa premeny zrkadlového obrazu na premenné hostiteľa prostredníctvom `cli/administration/inventory/provision/mirror_overrides.py`, ktorá znie `mirrors.yml.applications` a píše `applications.{role}.services.{service}.image` (a `.version`) do hostiteľských varov, ktoré sú predmetom služby `mirror_policy`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mode is read as ``compose_mode_force or DEPLOYMENT_MODE`` rather than the bare cluster mode, because ``container_networks`` resolves attachments through that same effective mode: a role with an override must not lose its pin and its overlay at once."
msgstr "Režim je čítaný ako ``compose_mode_force or DEPLOYMENT_MODE`` skôr než holým klastrom, pretože ``container_networks`` rieši prílohy tým istým účinným režimom: rola s prepisom nesmie stratiť svoj kolík a jeho prekrytie naraz."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mode selection is a *filter*, not an axis: ``--modes swarm`` keeps the rows whose role can be deployed as a swarm stack, ``--modes \"compose swarm\"`` keeps the rows at least one of the two can take. The shared filter is mode-clause + INFINITO_WHITELIST + INFINITO_BLACKLIST, the order is INFINITO_DISCOVERY_SORT, whose first key sorts clones last (one representative per dna cluster stays ahead of the budget cut, so redundant same-service-set variants fall behind it first), and the lifecycle envelope is INFINITO_LIFECYCLES."
msgstr "Výber režimu je *filter*, nie osi: ``--modes swarm`` udržiava riadky, ktorých úlohu možno nasadiť ako rojný kôš, ``--modes \"compose swarm\"`` udržuje riadky aspoň jeden z nich môže trvať. Zdieľaný filter je mode-clause + INFINITO_WHITELIST + INFINITO_BLACKLIST, poradie je INFINITO_DISCOVERY_SORT, ktorého prvé kľúčové druhy klonov posledný (jeden zástupca z jedného zoskupenia DNA zostáva pred znížením rozpočtu, takže nadbytočné varianty rovnakého súboru služieb za ním zapadajú ako prvé), a obálka životného cyklu je INFINITO_LIFECYCLES."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mode the guide would replay *app* in, or ``''`` when it cannot."
msgstr "Režim, ktorý by sprievodca prehral *Aplikácia* v, alebo ``''`` keď nemôže."

msgid "The model is reached through the model gateway, not through a model server, so the request carries a consumer identity and resolves through the gateway's model list like every other model call in this deployment."
msgstr ""

msgid "The models live in a separate repository `llm`, maintained by its own agent: a general base model fine-tuned on the operator's GPU, one LoRA adapter per persona, quantised to run on CPU, published with a pinned version. Core consumes them and builds nothing of them."
msgstr ""

msgid "The moderator mapping has no Playwright scenario: Ueberauth's Keycloak strategy maps no groups claim, so `users.role` follows a group change only when the `sys-ctl-mtn-rbac-sync` timer or a deploy runs `files/elixir/rbac.exs`, and a spec can trigger neither. Options: an upstream role mapping in the Keycloak strategy, or a spec that waits one timer interval after the group change."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The module is deliberately free of deploy-runtime imports: the CI selection resolves its closure on a runner that has no inventory, no container and no `INFINITO_SRC_DIR`."
msgstr "Modul je zámerne oslobodený od dovozu v čase rozmiestnenia: výber VOS vyrieši jeho uzavretie na bežcovi, ktorý nemá žiadny inventár, žiadny kontajner a žiadny `INFINITO_SRC_DIR`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The mount MUST be available before Docker starts. Otherwise the daemon may fall back to the system drive or fail to start cleanly."
msgstr "Montáž musí byť k dispozícii pred začatím Docker. V opačnom prípade sa démon môže vrátiť späť do systému pohonu alebo sa nepodarí začať čisto."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The name never holds a space: the ``whitelist`` and ``priority`` workflow inputs are space-separated lists, so a display name with a space in it would make a two-role list unparseable."
msgstr "Názov nikdy nemá priestor: ``whitelist`` a ``priority`` Vstupy pracovných tokov sú zoznamy oddelené od priestoru, takže zobrazovacie meno s priestorom v ňom by urobilo dvojúčelový zoznam neobsaditeľný."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The name of the matching role directory."
msgstr "Názov zoznamu zodpovedajúcich úloh."

msgid "The name search is a word match over the text, so a docstring or a comment naming a symbol counts as a consumer: the index errs towards a wider plan, never a narrower one. A plugin whose names cannot be read statically, or a group_vars file that does not parse, widens to the full set for the same reason."
msgstr ""

msgid "The name the update filters and the image lookup import it by."
msgstr ""

msgid "The named key, or ``\"\"`` when the binding names none and the card targets the primary domain."
msgstr ""

msgid "The named user MUST exist. The lookup raises for an unknown user, for a named user whose entry is no mapping, for a forward to the user itself and for a chain of forwards that loops. Role defaults and inventory overrides are checked alike; a `forward` that is still a Jinja expression is left to the mail provider, which reads it rendered."
msgstr ""

msgid "The named volumes ``plugins`` and ``client-plugins`` declared in ``meta/volumes.yml`` are node-local derived copies that every replica extracts for itself from the image’s prepackaged bundles; an uploaded bundle persists in the file store, not in them."
msgstr ""

msgid "The named volumes `plugins` and `client-plugins` declared in `meta/volumes.yml` are node-local derived copies that every replica extracts for itself from the image's prepackaged bundles; an uploaded bundle persists in the file store, not in them."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
