msgid "The two inputs a retrigger decides itself rather than carrying over."
msgstr "O dvoch vstupoch sa skôr rozhodne retraktivátor ako prenos."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The two measured inputs resolve in a fixed order: an inventory override (`RESOURCE_HOST_CPUS_OVERRIDE` / `RESOURCE_HOST_MEM_MB_OVERRIDE`), then the host's own hardware facts, then a probe of the machine this plugin runs on. The probe only applies to a target reached over the local connection, because a lookup executes on the Ansible controller: probing for a remote host would report the controller's hardware. That case raises and names the override to set."
msgstr "Dva namerané vstupy sa riešia v pevnom poradí: prepísanie zásob (`RESOURCE_HOST_CPUS_OVERRIDE` / `RESOURCE_HOST_MEM_MB_OVERRIDE`), potom hostiteľ vlastné hardvérové fakty, potom sonda stroja tento plugin beží na. Sonda sa vzťahuje len na cieľ, ktorý sa dosiahol cez miestne spojenie, pretože vyhľadávanie vykonáva na ovládači Ansible: sondovanie na vzdialenom hostiteľovi by nahlásilo hardvér regulátora. Ten prípad vyvolá a nastaví prepis."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The two mutual-exclusion guards (*tests/integration/iam/oauth2_oidc/test_mutual_exclusive.py*, *test_acl_mutual_exclusive.py*) — obsolete under the single-block schema."
msgstr "Dva vzájomné vylučovacie stráže (*tests/integration/iam/oauth2_oidc/test_mutual_exclusive.py*, *test_acl_mutual_exclusive.py*)."

msgid "The two sides of one diff."
msgstr ""

msgid "The two wired pairs ship as 026 addons. The four open ones stay open rather than being faked: wiring them would mean either writing the app plugin in this repository or giving the gateway a second dialect, and decision 2 pins it to the LibreTranslate API. An OpenAI-compatible route on the gateway would reach Nextcloud and Moodle in one move and is the obvious follow-up, recorded here rather than implemented."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The unified `# noqa` / `# nocheck` syntax that suppresses individual checks across the infinito-nexus test suite."
msgstr "Jednotná `# noqa` / `# nocheck` syntax, ktorá potláča jednotlivé kontroly cez infinito-nexus test suite."

msgid "The unified mode writes ``~/.claude/settings.json``, the editor’s default settings and the named Claude profile from the inventory. ``services.code.settings`` owns the general editor settings, including ``window.autoDetectColorScheme`` and the preferred light/dark themes. ``unified.settings`` owns other Claude settings; ``env``, ``model``, ``modelPicker``, and ``apiKeyHelper`` are reserved for the connection switch. Manual settings in these managed files are replaced without backups. Saved OAuth credentials, sessions, memories, and other user data are not settings and are retained. Retired profiles disappear from the profile registry, and their workspace associations move to the unified profile. The built-in Code Default profile remains available."
msgstr ""

msgid "The unified mode writes `~/.claude/settings.json`, the editor's default settings and the named Claude profile from the inventory. `services.code.settings` owns the general editor settings, including `window.autoDetectColorScheme` and the preferred light/dark themes. `unified.settings` owns other Claude settings; `env`, `model`, `modelPicker`, and `apiKeyHelper` are reserved for the connection switch. Manual settings in these managed files are replaced without backups. Saved OAuth credentials, sessions, memories, and other user data are not settings and are retained. Retired profiles disappear from the profile registry, and their workspace associations move to the unified profile. The built-in Code Default profile remains available."
msgstr ""

