msgid "The wiki's bureaucrat and sysop is the platform administrator's account, which `files/shell/realign_admin_password.sh` in `tasks/04_admin.yml` creates through `maintenance/run.php createAndPromote` only while local login is on. With `sso` on, `$wgPluggableAuth_EnableLocalLogin` is false, the script sends no password and leaves a missing account to its first OIDC login, which `$wgOpenIDConnect_MigrateUsersByUserName` links to an existing account of the same name. The script promotes an existing account that is no sysop to sysop and bureaucrat only while local login is off and its email, which PluggableAuth confirms when it creates the account, equals `MEDIAWIKI_ADMINISTRATOR_EMAIL`; otherwise the deploy fails and names the reason (local login on, email differs, email unconfirmed). `files/playwright/test-rbac-groups.js` asserts the group sync: it adds biber to each role group, signs in through Keycloak, reads the wiki groups from `Special:ListUsers`, then removes the membership and asserts the next login revokes them. It also signs the administrator in and asserts the session belongs to the provisioned account and holds `sysop`, `bureaucrat` and `interface-admin`. `files/playwright/test-profile-sync.js` sets `locale` and `zoneinfo` on biber in Keycloak, signs in, and asserts the interface language, the disabled preference fields on `Special:Preferences` and the saved `language` and `timecorrection` options."
msgstr ""

msgid "The wiki’s bureaucrat and sysop is the platform administrator’s account, which ``files/shell/realign_admin_password.sh`` in ``tasks/04_admin.yml`` creates through ``maintenance/run.php createAndPromote`` only while local login is on. With ``sso`` on, ``$wgPluggableAuth_EnableLocalLogin`` is false, the script sends no password and leaves a missing account to its first OIDC login, which ``$wgOpenIDConnect_MigrateUsersByUserName`` links to an existing account of the same name. The script promotes an existing account that is no sysop to sysop and bureaucrat only while local login is off and its email, which PluggableAuth confirms when it creates the account, equals ``MEDIAWIKI_ADMINISTRATOR_EMAIL``; otherwise the deploy fails and names the reason (local login on, email differs, email unconfirmed). ``files/playwright/test-rbac-groups.js`` asserts the group sync: it adds biber to each role group, signs in through Keycloak, reads the wiki groups from ``Special:ListUsers``, then removes the membership and asserts the next login revokes them. It also signs the administrator in and asserts the session belongs to the provisioned account and holds ``sysop``, ``bureaucrat`` and ``interface-admin``. ``files/playwright/test-profile-sync.js`` sets ``locale`` and ``zoneinfo`` on biber in Keycloak, signs in, and asserts the interface language, the disabled preference fields on ``Special:Preferences`` and the saved ``language`` and ``timecorrection`` options."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The wildcard in the namespace slot collapses 21 mutating verbs across `gh issue/pr/release/repo/ruleset/run/cache/gist/label/project/…` into a single rule per verb. Future namespaces that ship the same verb (e.g. a hypothetical `gh discussion lock`) are caught automatically. Explicit per-namespace lists rot as the `gh` CLI grows."
msgstr "Divoká karta v slote názvu sa zrúti 21 mutácia slovies cez `gh issue/pr/release/repo/ruleset/run/cache/gist/label/project/…` do jedného pravidla na sloveso. Budúce menové priestory, ktoré vysielajú rovnaké sloveso (napr. hypotetický `gh discussion lock`) sa chytia automaticky. Explicitné pre-namespace zoznamy hniť ako `gh` CLI rastie."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The window's start is the floor: with nothing green behind it the answer is the start itself, never the head. Walking back to the head is what made every retrigger redeploy the whole stretch its predecessors had already proven."
msgstr "Začiatok okna je podlaha: s ničím zeleným za ním odpoveď je samotný štart, nikdy hlava. Chôdza späť do hlavy je to, čo robil každý retrigger znovuzamestnať celý úsek jeho predchodcovia už preukázané."

msgid "The wired and declared layers are exhaustive by construction — they are read from the repository. The open layer is not: it grows as each role's upstream plugin ecosystem is surveyed. A MediaWiki survey, for example, surfaced `DiscourseSsoConsumer`, `PeerTubeEmbed`, `MachineTranslation` (libretranslate), `Extension:AWS` (minio) and an LLM editor (openwebui) — five integrations that no list had carried before someone looked."
