msgid "Turning an app's own `2fa` off, or `enforced: false`, after the deploy enforced it clears that enforcement by one of two rules. Where the app's second factor stays usable, the deploy clears only what an ownership marker says it switched on itself: Nextcloud (`occ config:app:get infinito twofactor_enforced_by_deploy`, and only while `occ` reports exactly \"enforced for all users\") and Odoo (`ir.config_parameter` `infinito.auth_totp_policy_by_deploy`, which also keeps the policy the deploy replaced and restores it); an enforcement an admin set stays. Where turning `2fa` off leaves no usable second factor, the deploy clears any enforcement, also one an admin set: Discourse (no local logins, so second-factor setup answers NotFound), EspoCRM, ERPNext, Gitea (with `passkey` also off), Joomla once no `multifactorauth` plugin is enabled any more, Nextcloud while no provider app is enabled, and Zammad, where the enforcement would be dormant until a method comes back. Joomla break-glass for a forced list without an enabled method: the SQL in its README on `<prefix>extensions.params`."
