msgid "ejabberd's only HTTP surface is `ejabberd_web_admin` on `/admin` (see [`templates/configuration.yml.j2`](./templates/configuration.yml.j2)). It authenticates a bare JID against LDAP over HTTP Basic, so there is no Keycloak redirect to follow and no in-app logout control to click; client authentication itself runs over ports 5222/5269 and stays outside the Playwright loop, as noted under Watch Points. `acl.admin` lists only the platform administrator and the members of the `administrator` role, so the web admin refuses every other account outright. [`templates/playwright.env.j2`](./templates/playwright.env.j2) therefore declares `PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true` and `PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`; the `guest` persona and the baseline reachability assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "ejabberd’s ``mod_admin`` HTTP UI is the only Playwright-testable surface; XMPP client login itself runs over 5222/5269 and MUST be exercised by an XMPP-aware client outside the Playwright test loop."
msgstr "ejabberd ``mod_admin`` HTTP UI je jediný Playwright-testable povrch; XMPP klient login sám beží cez 5222/5269 a MUSÍ ho vykonávať XMPP-Vedomý klient mimo testovacej slučky Playwright."

msgid "ejabberd’s only HTTP surface is ``ejabberd_web_admin`` on ``/admin`` (see ```templates/configuration.yml.j2`` <./templates/configuration.yml.j2>`__). It authenticates a bare JID against LDAP over HTTP Basic, so there is no Keycloak redirect to follow and no in-app logout control to click; client authentication itself runs over ports 5222/5269 and stays outside the Playwright loop, as noted under Watch Points. ``acl.admin`` lists only the platform administrator and the members of the ``administrator`` role, so the web admin refuses every other account outright. ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ therefore declares ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``; the ``guest`` persona and the baseline reachability assertions run unconditionally."
